course: dictionary
lesson: 965
title: One word, many meanings: blue
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word blue can mean a colour, a feeling, or a phrase. The words around it show you which meaning is right. «The sky was clear and blue over the sea.» Here blue is a colour, because skies and seas have colours.
explain: «Out of the blue» is not about colour at all. It means suddenly, with no warning. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have found it.
explain: «Feeling blue» means feeling sad, and «once in a blue moon» means very rarely. These phrases do not mean what the single words mean, so when a sentence sounds odd, look at the other words for clues, then ask a dictionary if you are still stuck.
fact: Blue is a primary colour, and it is the colour of a clear sky or the sea.
fact: «Feeling blue» means feeling sad.
fact: «Out of the blue» means suddenly, without warning.
fact: «Once in a blue moon» means very rarely.
fact: «Blues» can also be a kind of slow, sad music.
exercise: «Stars have different colours: the hottest are blue-white, our Sun is yellow-white.» In this sentence, blue describes a colour. What colour is it like? | *A clear, bright colour like the sky | Very rarely seen | A sad, gloomy feeling | A loud noise
exercise: «He arrived out of the blue, without any warning.» What does out of the blue mean? | Out of the sea | Very slowly | Very rarely | *Suddenly, without warning
exercise: Sara says, «I am feeling blue today.» What does feeling blue mean? | Feeling cold | Feeling tall | Feeling hungry | *Feeling sad
test: «A newborn blue whale can gain about 90 kilograms a day.» What is a blue whale? | A type of cloud | A small blue bird | A sad song | *A huge sea animal
test: «We only go to the beach once in a blue moon.» What does once in a blue moon mean? | Every night | Always on sunny days | *Very rarely | Every month
exam: Which phrase means very rarely? | *Once in a blue moon | Out of the blue | Blue whale | Feeling blue
